{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00575",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.98,
      "end_seconds": 6.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "G'day. What should I call you, Mr Whitlock or something less formal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.58,
      "end_seconds": 19.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "Darren's good. Look, I'm a bit freaked out. There's this ringing in my left ear and it won't stop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.55,
      "end_seconds": 25.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Okay, Darren. How long's it been going?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.66,
      "end_seconds": 36.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Three days now. Started on Sunday arvo while I was out in the yard."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.47,
      "end_seconds": 40.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Constant, or on and off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.94,
      "end_seconds": 51.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Pretty much constant. It goes quiet when the telly's on, but at night it's really loud."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.11,
      "end_seconds": 60.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "What does it sound like? A hiss, a buzz, a beep?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.51,
      "end_seconds": 68.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.63,
      "text": "More like a high whistle. Like a kettle that never quite boils."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.19,
      "end_seconds": 78.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Right. Anything else going on in that ear? Blocked, sore, fluid coming out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.65,
      "end_seconds": 90.92,
      "duration_seconds": 9.27,
      "text": "It feels sort of muffled, like I've got cotton wool in there. That's new too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.6,
      "end_seconds": 97.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Muffled on the left only?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.97,
      "end_seconds": 104.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Yeah, just the left. The right ear's perfect."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.35,
      "end_seconds": 111.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Any spinning or dizziness with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.5,
      "end_seconds": 124.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "No, thank god. I'd have gone straight to emergency. Is this something awful? My neighbour had a tumour thing on his hearing nerve."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.48,
      "end_seconds": 137.4,
      "duration_seconds": 10.92,
      "text": "That's very uncommon, and it doesn't usually come on over a weekend. Let's have a proper look first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.1,
      "end_seconds": 144.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Okay. Should I be worried about going deaf in that ear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.26,
      "end_seconds": 153.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Let me look before I answer that. Keep still for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.41,
      "end_seconds": 184.25,
      "duration_seconds": 14.84,
      "text": "Left ear canal is partly blocked by a plug of wax. The eardrum behind it looks normal and intact, from what I can see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.46,
      "end_seconds": 190.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Wax? That's it? I've been losing sleep over wax?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.49,
      "end_seconds": 201.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.38,
      "text": "Wax can press on the eardrum and cause ringing and that muffled feeling. It's common."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.9,
      "end_seconds": 209.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "I've never had it before, though. I don't even use cotton buds much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.38,
      "end_seconds": 219.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Even occasionally is enough to pack it in. Best to stop using them altogether."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.58,
      "end_seconds": 228.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Right. And do I need drops, or does somebody syringe it out?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.05,
      "end_seconds": 242.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.64,
      "text": "We can go over that next visit if it doesn't clear. For now, keep the ear dry in the shower and leave it alone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.28,
      "end_seconds": 250.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "How dry? Like a shower cap on my head?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.47,
      "end_seconds": 261.72,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "A bit of cotton wool with Vaseline on it in the outer ear is plenty. Don't poke anything in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.3,
      "end_seconds": 274.34,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Fair enough. My missus swears by those ear candle things, though. She wants me to try one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.88,
      "end_seconds": 284.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Skip them. They don't draw wax out, and I've seen a few nasty burns from them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.48,
      "end_seconds": 294.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.36,
      "text": "I'll tell her the doctor said no. She'll argue, but I'll tell her anyway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.12,
      "end_seconds": 304.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "Blame me, that's what I'm here for. Anything else on your mind before we wrap up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.13,
      "end_seconds": 314.51,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Okay. Before I forget, you probably want to know about allergies. I've got none."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.98,
      "end_seconds": 322.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "Good, no allergies, thanks for saying so. Pop that in the notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.38,
      "end_seconds": 333.78,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "And when will the ringing stop? If it's wax, will it be gone straight away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.93,
      "end_seconds": 347.02,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "It should ease over a week or so as the wax shifts. If it's still ringing in two weeks, come back and see me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.38,
      "end_seconds": 355.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "And if the hearing drops off completely, or I get dizzy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.66,
      "end_seconds": 367.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Then ring the clinic the same day. Sudden loss in one ear is something we act on quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.6,
      "end_seconds": 374.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Got it. Thanks, doc. I'll sleep better tonight."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.91,
      "end_seconds": 379.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Good. Cheers, Darren."
    }
  ]
}
